.TH SHARDPOSTCTL-SERVER 1 "2026-10-03" "ShardPost 0.52.0" "ShardPost Manual"
.SH NAME
shardpostctl-server \- version, state and registrations of ShardPost servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shardpostctl version
.br
.B shardpostctl server status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl server list
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The commands ask the server about itself and about the processes
registered in the store. None touches an account.
.SS version
Prints the version of the server the client is talking to and the Go
version it was built with. Use it to check which build answers on this
socket or endpoint, for example after a rollout.
.PP
Role:
.BR diagnose .
.SS server status
Prints the state of this one server process:
.TP
.B version
Server version.
.TP
.B instance
Name of the process, in the cluster the pod name. Two pods serve the
same accounts, so the same command can answer from either one.
.TP
.B started
When the process started.
.TP
.B config fingerprint
Hash over the effective configuration, with secrets left out. Two
servers that answer with different fingerprints run different
configurations, which is almost always a rollout that did not finish.
.TP
.B store
Result of a ping against the RADOS store, plus the pools in use.
.TP
.B placement
Where the store's own namespaces (admin store, account directory,
queues) live, as the server's last placement check found it:
.B none
(the index pool),
.B native
or
.B migrated
(the system pool of
.IR ceph.system_pool ,
initialized there or migrated there, with its name and pool id), or
.B unknown
(the last check could not read; the server goes on). A server checks
it every minute and ends when it reads a placement that contradicts its
configuration.
.PP
Requires the role
.BR diagnose .
.SS server list
Lists the registrations of the processes that use the store, one line
per instance: every server, every job runner, the JMAP push workers,
scrubs, sweeps and backfills register at startup and every minute
.RB ( servers/<instance>
in the admin store) and record their orderly end. Columns:
.TP
.B INSTANCE
The pod name for a server;
.IB host \-push
for the JMAP push worker and
.IB host \-runner
for a job runner (both stable across restarts of their container);
.IB host \- role \- random
for the other processes, which may run in a server's pod.
.TP
.B ROLE
.BR serve ,
.B runner
(a job runner pod,
.BR "shardpost runner" ),
.BR push ,
.BR scrub ,
.B backfill
or
.BR sweep ;
.B "serve (before 0.47)"
for a registration without a role.
.TP
.B VERSION
The version of the process.
.TP
.B SYSTEM POOL
The system pool the process works with, by name and id;
.B \-
when the store's own namespaces live in the index pool.
.TP
.B RUNNING
.B true
while the registration was renewed within three minutes and the
process has not ended in order. A process that crashed stays
.B true
for up to three minutes after its last heartbeat.
.TP
.BR SEEN ", " STARTED ", " STOPPED
The last heartbeat, the start of the process and its orderly end
.RB ( \-
while it runs or after a crash).
.TP
.B WORKERS
For a server: whether it runs the background workers (the job runner,
the expiry workers, the delayed submission worker, the learning
worker), that is
.I workers.run
.RB ( WORKERS_RUN ).
.B false
is a front-end in a deployment with job runners;
.B \-
for the other roles and for servers before 0.52.0.
.TP
.BR PARTITIONS ", " WATCHED
For the JMAP push worker: the push partitions it holds (of 64) and
the accounts with push subscriptions it watches, as of its last
heartbeat;
.B \-
for the other roles. The partitions of all fresh push workers together
should reach 64; see
.IR docs/jmap.md .
.PP
A registration not renewed for 24 hours is deleted. With
.I admin.kv_index
other than
.B read
the command lists the admin namespace. Requires the role
.BR diagnose .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the answer as JSON instead of a table.
.SH EXAMPLES
What runs against the store right now, with which role and system pool?
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl server list
shardpostctl server list \-\-json | jq \-r '.servers[] | select(.fresh) | .instance'
.RE
.fi
.PP
Do the push workers hold every partition between them?
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl server list \-\-json \\
    | jq '[.servers[] | select(.fresh and .role == "push") | .partitions] | add'
.RE
.fi
.PP
Which build is live, and do both pods agree on their configuration?
.PP
.nf
.RS
for p in $(kubectl -n shardpost get pod \\
        -l app.kubernetes.io/name=shardpost-server -o name); do
    kubectl -n shardpost exec $p -c import -- \\
        shardpostctl server status
done
.RE
.fi
.PP
Version only, for a deployment check:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl version
.RE
.fi
.PP
Feed the state into a monitoring script:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl server status --json | jq -r '.store.ok, .config_fingerprint'
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The server answered.
.TP
.B 75
The server is not reachable, or
.B server list
asked a server without an admin store (the registrations are not
available there). A server that answers but cannot reach its
store is not a failure of the command: it prints
.I store unavailable
with the reason and exits 0 — that is the answer you asked for.
.TP
.B 77
The caller lacks the role
.BR diagnose .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shardpostctl (1),
.BR shardpostctl-account (1)
